From ed75e24bda373b74f1c65a8d0f4cfa374d1fdc66 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 21:44:17 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] gateway boot: resolve native-recovery route owners
 off the loop; batch the startup prune

Problem: the hub gateway's event loop stalls 3-7 s at every boot with
`loop top=hermes_state.py:1226 <lambda>` (SessionDB._read_one). In ~20 h of
hub loop-watch.jsonl (2026-11-13): 223 such stalls >= 3 s, 1,533 s in total.

Why 1: two boot paths do one full get_session() per routing entry on the loop:
  - recover_profile_native_sessions -> authority.logical_owner(entry.session_id)
    for every route (182 stalls, every 6-7 s one; e.g. 21:07:56 6.996 s, 39/40
    samples in get_compression_lineage -> get_session);
  - SessionStore._prune_stale_sessions_locked -> db.get_session per entry
    (41 stalls; e.g. 21:13:32 3.96 s, 16/30 samples).
Why 2: it is a slow query by volume, not a write-lock wait: the hub has 16,337
  routing entries (15,884 ended local kanban/cron/oneshot routes kept by the
  local-receipt rule), and get_session joins the resolved system prompt
  (~45 KB/row). Measured on hub state.db: 3,000 get_session-shaped reads 0.48 s
  raw vs 0.015 s for an id/parent/end_reason read; WAL readers never wait on
  the writer.
Why 3: the owner scan runs even when nothing is pending (session_admissions
  had 0 queued/unknown/started rows), and both scans sit on the loop thread.
Root (happened): boot recovery code scales O(routes) with full-row reads on
  the event loop, while the routing index only grows.
Root (not caught): tests used a handful of routes; nothing asserted the boot
  scan stays off the loop.

Fix:
- recover_profile_native_sessions: the admission read, checkpoint reads and
  route-owner resolution move into _pending_native_routes, run via
  asyncio.to_thread; the per-route scan is skipped when nothing is pending.
  Adapter lookup and recover_native_sessions stay on the loop.
- _prune_stale_sessions_locked: end reasons come from chunked
  `SELECT id, end_reason ... WHERE end_reason IS NOT NULL AND id IN (...)`
  reads per owning db; _stale_entry_verdict only reads row["end_reason"].
  Handles without _read_all (test doubles) keep the per-row get_session path.

Proof: tests/gateway/test_boot_recovery_off_loop.py fails 3/3 on the old code
(owner resolution on the loop thread; scan with nothing pending; prune calls
get_session per entry) and passes after. Existing prune, native-boot,
local-recovery and receipt suites (24 files, 194 tests) pass.
